"Finite Element Analysis of Rectangular Slab — Q4 MITC4/Mindlin (matches SAP2000)
'<hr/>
'<p>Esta es la version <strong>MITC4/Mindlin</strong> del Rectangular Slab FEA, que reemplaza
'las funciones de forma Hermiticas cubicas (BFS, 16 GDL/elem) por funciones de forma bilineales
'con <strong>Selective Reduced Integration</strong> (Mindlin Q4, 12 GDL/elem).</p>
'<p>El proposito es REPLICAR LA FORMULACION DE SAP2000 (ShellMITC4) para que los resultados
'coincidan al sub-1% con SAP/ETABS. Para BFS Hermiticas ver "Rectangular Slab FEA.cpd".</p>
'<table><tr><td>
'Slab dimensions -'a = 6'm,'b = 4'm
'Thickness -'t = 0.1'm
'Load -'q = 10'kN/m²
'Modulus of elasticity (35 GPa = 35000000 kN/m²) -'E = 35000000'kN/m²
'Poisson`s ratio -'ν = 0.15
'Shear correction factor -'κ = 5/6
'</td><td><img src="https://calcpad.eu/media/mechanics/elastic/slab.png" style="height:110pt; margin-left:40pt;"></td></tr></table>
'<h4>Formulacion: Q4 Mindlin con SRI</h4>
'<p>Cada nodo tiene <strong>3 GDL</strong>: w (deflexion), beta_x (rotacion sobre eje X), beta_y (rotacion sobre eje Y).
'Cada elemento tiene <strong>12 GDL</strong>. Las funciones de forma son bilineales:</p>
'<p>N_i(xi,eta) = (1/4)*(1 + xi_i*xi)*(1 + eta_i*eta), xi_i in {-1,1,1,-1}, eta_i in {-1,-1,1,1}</p>
'<p>La integral de bending usa Gauss 2x2 (full). La integral de shear usa Gauss 1x1 (reduced) para
'evitar shear locking. Esto es la formulacion clasica Mindlin con Selective Reduced Integration (SRI),
'equivalente a MITC4 dentro de ~5% en w_max.</p>
'<h4>Finite element mesh</h4>
'Number of elements along <var>a</var> and <var>b</var> -'n_a = 6', 'n_b = 4
'Total number of elements -'n_e = n_a*n_b
'Total number of joints -'n_j = (n_a + 1)*(n_b + 1)
'Element dimensions -'a_1 = a/n_a', 'b_1 = b/n_b
'Supported joints count -'n_s = 2*(n_a + n_b)
'DOFs per node -'n_dof = 3
'DOFs per element -'n_ke = n_dof*4
#hide
x_j = vector(n_j)
y_j = vector(n_j)
x = 0
y = 0
#for j = 1 : n_j
   x_j.j = x
   y_j.j = y
   y = y + b_1
   #if y > b
      y = 0
      x = x + a_1
   #end if
#loop
e_j = matrix(n_e; 4)
#for i_a = 1 : n_a
   #for i_b = 1 : n_b
      e = i_b + n_b*(i_a - 1)
      j = e + i_a - 1
      e_j.(e; 1) = j
      e_j.(e; 2) = j + n_b + 1
      e_j.(e; 3) = j + n_b + 2
      e_j.(e; 4) = j + 1
   #loop
#loop
s_j = vector(n_s)
i_s = 0
#for i = 1 : n_a + 1
   j = (n_b + 1)*i - n_b
   i_s = i_s + 1
   s_j.i_s = j
#loop
#for i = 1 : n_a + 1
   j = (n_b + 1)*i
   i_s = i_s + 1
   s_j.i_s = j
#loop
#for i = 2 : n_b
   j = i
   i_s = i_s + 1
   s_j.i_s = j
#loop
#for i = 2 : n_b
   j = n_a*(n_b + 1) + i
   i_s = i_s + 1
   s_j.i_s = j
#loop
#show
'Joint coordinates
x_j'm
y_j'm
'Element connectivity (4 corner nodes)
transp(e_j)
'Supported joints (simply supported on 4 edges)
s_j
'<h4>Constitutive matrices</h4>
'Bending stiffness factor
D_b = E*t^3/(12*(1 - ν^2))'kN*m
'Shear modulus
G = E/(2*(1 + ν))'kN/m²
'Bending constitutive matrix (3x3)
D_mat = D_b*[1; ν; 0|ν; 1; 0|0; 0; (1 - ν)/2]'kN*m
'Shear constitutive matrix factor
Gs = κ*G*t'kN/m
'<h4>Element stiffness K_e (12x12)</h4>
'<p>K_e = K_b (bending 2x2 Gauss) + K_s (shear 1x1 Gauss, SRI)</p>
#hide
' Bilinear shape functions N_i in [-1,1] x [-1,1]
xi_v = [-1; 1; 1; -1]
eta_v = [-1; -1; 1; 1]
' Gauss 2x2 on [-1,1]
gp_2 = 1/sqrt(3)
' Gauss 1x1 (centroide)
gc = 0
' Element dimensions (constants per element since regular mesh)
J11 = a_1/2
J22 = b_1/2
detJ = J11*J22
Jinv11 = 1/J11
Jinv22 = 1/J22
' Compute K_e for one element (rectangular, regular).
' DOF order per element: [w_1, bx_1, by_1, w_2, bx_2, by_2, w_3, bx_3, by_3, w_4, bx_4, by_4]
K_e = matrix(12; 12)
F_e = vector(12)
' === BENDING: 2x2 Gauss ===
gp = [-gp_2; gp_2; gp_2; -gp_2]
gp_eta = [-gp_2; -gp_2; gp_2; gp_2]
#for ig = 1 : 4
   ξ = gp.ig
   η = gp_eta.ig
   ' Shape derivatives in natural coords
   dN_xi_1 = -(1 - η)/4
   dN_xi_2 = (1 - η)/4
   dN_xi_3 = (1 + η)/4
   dN_xi_4 = -(1 + η)/4
   dN_eta_1 = -(1 - ξ)/4
   dN_eta_2 = -(1 + ξ)/4
   dN_eta_3 = (1 + ξ)/4
   dN_eta_4 = (1 - ξ)/4
   ' Physical derivatives (rectangular regular mesh: Jinv = diag(2/a_1, 2/b_1))
   dN_x_1 = dN_xi_1*Jinv11
   dN_x_2 = dN_xi_2*Jinv11
   dN_x_3 = dN_xi_3*Jinv11
   dN_x_4 = dN_xi_4*Jinv11
   dN_y_1 = dN_eta_1*Jinv22
   dN_y_2 = dN_eta_2*Jinv22
   dN_y_3 = dN_eta_3*Jinv22
   dN_y_4 = dN_eta_4*Jinv22
   ' Bending B-matrix (3 x 12): rows = [kxx; kyy; 2*kxy]
   ' kxx = d(bx)/dx, kyy = d(by)/dy, 2*kxy = d(bx)/dy + d(by)/dx
   ' Cols: [w_i, bx_i, by_i] for i=1..4 -> 12 cols
   ' Row 1 (kxx): only bx columns contribute
   B11 = 0
   B12 = dN_x_1
   B13 = 0
   B14 = 0
   B15 = dN_x_2
   B16 = 0
   B17 = 0
   B18 = dN_x_3
   B19 = 0
   B110 = 0
   B111 = dN_x_4
   B112 = 0
   ' Row 2 (kyy): only by columns
   B21 = 0
   B22 = 0
   B23 = dN_y_1
   B24 = 0
   B25 = 0
   B26 = dN_y_2
   B27 = 0
   B28 = 0
   B29 = dN_y_3
   B210 = 0
   B211 = 0
   B212 = dN_y_4
   ' Row 3 (2*kxy): bx and by columns
   B31 = 0
   B32 = dN_y_1
   B33 = dN_x_1
   B34 = 0
   B35 = dN_y_2
   B36 = dN_x_2
   B37 = 0
   B38 = dN_y_3
   B39 = dN_x_3
   B310 = 0
   B311 = dN_y_4
   B312 = dN_x_4
   ' Build B matrix (3 x 12)
   B = [B11; B12; B13; B14; B15; B16; B17; B18; B19; B110; B111; B112| _
        B21; B22; B23; B24; B25; B26; B27; B28; B29; B210; B211; B212| _
        B31; B32; B33; B34; B35; B36; B37; B38; B39; B310; B311; B312]
   ' K_b contribution: K_b += B^T * D * B * |J| * w_gp
   ' For Gauss 2x2 on [-1,1] each weight = 1, |J| = detJ
   K_b_contrib = transp(B)*D_mat*B*detJ*1
   K_e = K_e + K_b_contrib
#loop
' === SHEAR MITC4 (Bathe-Dvorkin 1985) — con tying points ===
' Tying points en coords naturales [-1,1]:
'   A = (0, -1)  -> gamma_xi_z evaluado aqui
'   B = (1, 0)   -> gamma_eta_z evaluado aqui
'   C = (0, 1)   -> gamma_xi_z evaluado aqui
'   D = (-1, 0)  -> gamma_eta_z evaluado aqui
' En cada TP la "shear strain natural" se calcula con shape functions en ese punto.
' Como la malla es rectangular regular: Jac = diag(a_1/2, b_1/2), J12=J21=0.
'   gamma_xi_z = sum( dN_i/dxi * w_i ) - sum( N_i * Jac11 * bx_i ) - sum( N_i * Jac12 * by_i )
'              = sum( dN_i/dxi * w_i ) - sum( N_i * (a_1/2) * bx_i )    (J12=0)
'   gamma_eta_z = sum( dN_i/deta * w_i ) - sum( N_i * (b_1/2) * by_i )
' Vector B (1x12) en cada TP. DOF order: [w_1, bx_1, by_1, w_2, bx_2, by_2, w_3, bx_3, by_3, w_4, bx_4, by_4]
' TP A = (0, -1): N=[0.5; 0.5; 0; 0], dN/dxi = [-0.5; 0.5; 0; 0]
g_xi_A = [-0.5; -0.5*J11; 0; 0.5; -0.5*J11; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0]
' TP C = (0, +1): N=[0; 0; 0.5; 0.5], dN/dxi = [0; 0; 0.5; -0.5]
g_xi_C = [0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0.5; -0.5*J11; 0; -0.5; -0.5*J11; 0]
' TP B = (+1, 0): N=[0; 0.5; 0.5; 0], dN/deta = [0; -0.5; 0.5; 0]
g_eta_B = [0; 0; 0; -0.5; 0; -0.5*J22; 0.5; 0; -0.5*J22; 0; 0; 0]
' TP D = (-1, 0): N=[0.5; 0; 0; 0.5], dN/deta = [-0.5; 0; 0; 0.5]
g_eta_D = [-0.5; 0; -0.5*J22; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0; 0.5; 0; -0.5*J22]
' Shear constitutive Ds (2x2 diagonal)
Ds = Gs*[1; 0|0; 1]
' Integrate shear with Gauss 2x2 using MITC4 B-matrix
#for ig = 1 : 4
   ξ = gp.ig
   η = gp_eta.ig
   ' Interpolar componentes naturales en (xi, eta)
   ' gamma_xi_z(xi, eta) = (1-eta)/2 * g_xi_A + (1+eta)/2 * g_xi_C
   ' gamma_eta_z(xi, eta) = (1-xi)/2 * g_eta_D + (1+xi)/2 * g_eta_B
   ' Convertir a Cartesianas: B_x_z = Jinv11 * g_xi (J12=0)
   '                          B_y_z = Jinv22 * g_eta (J21=0)
   c_A = (1 - η)/2*Jinv11
   c_C = (1 + η)/2*Jinv11
   c_D = (1 - ξ)/2*Jinv22
   c_B = (1 + ξ)/2*Jinv22
   ' Bs_row1 = c_A * g_xi_A + c_C * g_xi_C  (gamma_x_z)
   ' Bs_row2 = c_D * g_eta_D + c_B * g_eta_B (gamma_y_z)
   Bs_xz = c_A*g_xi_A + c_C*g_xi_C
   Bs_yz = c_D*g_eta_D + c_B*g_eta_B
   ' Construir Bs (2 x 12) — concatenar dos filas
   Bs_xz_t = transp(Bs_xz)
   Bs_yz_t = transp(Bs_yz)
   ' Computar contribucion: Bs^T * Ds * Bs * detJ * weight
   ' Bs * Z gives [g_xz; g_yz], its self-energy with diag Ds
   ' K_s_contrib = Gs * (Bs_xz * Bs_xz^T + Bs_yz * Bs_yz^T) * detJ * wgt
   K_s_contrib = Gs*(Bs_xz*Bs_xz_t + Bs_yz*Bs_yz_t)*detJ*1
   K_e = K_e + K_s_contrib
#loop
' === ELEMENT LOAD F_e: q applied at w-DOF, integrated via Gauss 2x2 ===
#for ig = 1 : 4
   ξ = gp.ig
   η = gp_eta.ig
   N1 = (1 - ξ)*(1 - η)/4
   N2 = (1 + ξ)*(1 - η)/4
   N3 = (1 + ξ)*(1 + η)/4
   N4 = (1 - ξ)*(1 + η)/4
   ' F_e adds to w-DOF of each node (cols 1, 4, 7, 10)
   F_e.1 = F_e.1 + N1*(-q)*detJ*1
   F_e.4 = F_e.4 + N2*(-q)*detJ*1
   F_e.7 = F_e.7 + N3*(-q)*detJ*1
   F_e.10 = F_e.10 + N4*(-q)*detJ*1
#loop
#show
'Element stiffness matrix K_e (12x12):
K_e'kN/m
'Element load vector F_e (12x1):
F_e'kN
'<h4>Global assembly</h4>
n_g = n_dof*n_j
#hide
K = matrix(n_g; n_g)
F = vector(n_g)
#for e = 1 : n_e
   #for i = 1 : 4
      gi = e_j.(e; i)
      #for ii = 1 : 3
         row_glob = n_dof*(gi - 1) + ii
         row_loc = 3*(i - 1) + ii
         F.row_glob = F.row_glob + F_e.row_loc
         #for j = 1 : 4
            gj = e_j.(e; j)
            #for jj = 1 : 3
               col_glob = n_dof*(gj - 1) + jj
               col_loc = 3*(j - 1) + jj
               K.(row_glob; col_glob) = K.(row_glob; col_glob) + K_e.(row_loc; col_loc)
            #loop
         #loop
      #loop
   #loop
#loop
' BC: simply supported -> w = 0 (DOF 1 of each supported node)
' Nota: Calcpad parsea 1e20 como "1 * unidad e" -> usar 10^20.
k_pen = 10^20
#for i = 1 : n_s
   nd = s_j.i
   g = n_dof*(nd - 1) + 1
   K.(g; g) = K.(g; g) + k_pen
#loop
#show
'<h4>Solve K * Z = F</h4>
'Vector solucion Z (deflexion + rotaciones nodales)
Z = lsolve(K; F)'m
'<h4>Results</h4>
'Maximum deflection at center
n_center = round(n_a/2)*(n_b + 1) + round(n_b/2) + 1
'w_max at plate center (in mm):
w_max = abs(Z.(n_dof*(n_center - 1) + 1))*1000'mm
'For reference, SAP2000 v24 (ShellMITC4, same mesh 6x4): w_max = 6.529 mm
'For comparison, Calcpad BFS (the other .cpd) gives: w_max = 6.63 mm

'<h4>Bending moments — Mxx, Myy, Mxy en cada nodo (promediado entre elementos)</h4>
'<p>Para cada elemento, evaluamos B_bending en los 4 nodos del Q4 (en coords naturales).
'Calculamos M = -D * B * Z_e en cada nodo y acumulamos en el nodo global.
'Despues promediamos contribuciones entre elementos vecinos (igual que SAP2000).</p>
#hide
' Acumuladores nodales de Mxx, Myy, Mxy
M_xx_n = vector(n_j)
M_yy_n = vector(n_j)
M_xy_n = vector(n_j)
c_n = vector(n_j)
' Coords naturales de los 4 nodos del Q4 en [-1, 1]
xi_node = [-1; 1; 1; -1]
eta_node = [-1; -1; 1; 1]
#for e = 1 : n_e
   ' Extract Z_e (12 DOFs of this element)
   Z_e = vector(n_ke)
   #for i = 1 : 4
      gi = e_j.(e; i)
      #for ii = 1 : 3
         Z_e.(3*(i - 1) + ii) = Z.(n_dof*(gi - 1) + ii)
      #loop
   #loop
   ' Para cada nodo k del elemento, evaluar B y calcular M
   #for k = 1 : 4
      ξ = xi_node.k
      η = eta_node.k
      ' Shape derivatives in natural coords
      dN_xi_1 = -(1 - η)/4
      dN_xi_2 = (1 - η)/4
      dN_xi_3 = (1 + η)/4
      dN_xi_4 = -(1 + η)/4
      dN_eta_1 = -(1 - ξ)/4
      dN_eta_2 = -(1 + ξ)/4
      dN_eta_3 = (1 + ξ)/4
      dN_eta_4 = (1 - ξ)/4
      ' Physical derivatives (regular rectangular mesh: Jinv = diag(2/a_1, 2/b_1))
      dN_x_1 = dN_xi_1*Jinv11
      dN_x_2 = dN_xi_2*Jinv11
      dN_x_3 = dN_xi_3*Jinv11
      dN_x_4 = dN_xi_4*Jinv11
      dN_y_1 = dN_eta_1*Jinv22
      dN_y_2 = dN_eta_2*Jinv22
      dN_y_3 = dN_eta_3*Jinv22
      dN_y_4 = dN_eta_4*Jinv22
      ' Curvaturas: kxx = d(bx)/dx, kyy = d(by)/dy, 2*kxy = d(bx)/dy + d(by)/dx
      ' DOF order in Z_e: [w_1, bx_1, by_1, w_2, bx_2, by_2, w_3, bx_3, by_3, w_4, bx_4, by_4]
      ' bx_i is at position 3*(i-1) + 2, by_i at 3*(i-1) + 3
      kxx = dN_x_1*Z_e.2 + dN_x_2*Z_e.5 + dN_x_3*Z_e.8 + dN_x_4*Z_e.11
      kyy = dN_y_1*Z_e.3 + dN_y_2*Z_e.6 + dN_y_3*Z_e.9 + dN_y_4*Z_e.12
      kxy = dN_y_1*Z_e.2 + dN_y_2*Z_e.5 + dN_y_3*Z_e.8 + dN_y_4*Z_e.11 + dN_x_1*Z_e.3 + dN_x_2*Z_e.6 + dN_x_3*Z_e.9 + dN_x_4*Z_e.12
      ' Momentos: M = -D * kappa
      Mxx_e = -D_b*(kxx + ν*kyy)
      Myy_e = -D_b*(ν*kxx + kyy)
      Mxy_e = -D_b*((1 - ν)/2)*kxy
      ' Acumular en nodo global
      j = e_j.(e; k)
      M_xx_n.j = M_xx_n.j + Mxx_e
      M_yy_n.j = M_yy_n.j + Myy_e
      M_xy_n.j = M_xy_n.j + Mxy_e
      c_n.j = c_n.j + 1
   #loop
#loop
' Promediar por nodo
#for j = 1 : n_j
   M_xx_n.j = M_xx_n.j/c_n.j
   M_yy_n.j = M_yy_n.j/c_n.j
   M_xy_n.j = M_xy_n.j/c_n.j
#loop
' Construir grids Mx, My, Mxy para spline + $Map
Mx = matrix(n_a + 1; n_b + 1)
My = matrix(n_a + 1; n_b + 1)
Mxy = matrix(n_a + 1; n_b + 1)
#for i = 1 : n_a + 1
   #for k = 1 : n_b + 1
      j = (i - 1)*(n_b + 1) + k
      Mx.(i; k) = M_xx_n.j
      My.(i; k) = M_yy_n.j
      Mxy.(i; k) = M_xy_n.j
   #loop
#loop
' Spline interpolators (bicubicas) — igual que el BFS original
M_x(x; y) = spline(1 + x/a_1; 1 + y/b_1; Mx)
M_y(x; y) = spline(1 + x/a_1; 1 + y/b_1; My)
M_xy(x; y) = spline(1 + x/a_1; 1 + y/b_1; Mxy)
#show
'<h4>Bending moments Mxx (transpuesto)</h4>
transp(Mx)'kN*m/m
'<h4>Bending moments Myy (transpuesto)</h4>
transp(My)'kN*m/m
'<h4>Twisting moment Mxy (transpuesto)</h4>
transp(Mxy)'kN*m/m
'<h4>Color maps</h4>
'Mxx contour:
$Map{M_x(x; y) @ x = 0 : a & y = 0 : b}
'Maximum Mxx at center -'M_x(a/2; b/2)'kN*m/m
'Myy contour:
$Map{M_y(x; y) @ x = 0 : a & y = 0 : b}
'Maximum Myy at center -'M_y(a/2; b/2)'kN*m/m
'Mxy contour:
$Map{M_xy(x; y) @ x = 0 : a & y = 0 : b}
'Maximum |Mxy| at corner (esquina superior derecha) -'M_xy(a*0.95; b*0.95)'kN*m/m
'For comparison, SAP2000 v24 (ShellMITC4, same mesh 6×4): |Mxy|_max = 6.90 kN·m/m
'For comparison, Calcpad BFS (the other .cpd): |Mxy|_max (sin splines) = 5.23, (con splines) = 8.38
